  "sections": {
    "4b11c6f9": {
      "body": "Mia is Swahili for 100. The mark is a field of a hundred dots, ten by ten, with about ten of them lit: a hundred places for your branches, a few of them in use. It is drawn as circles only, in one colour, ink #191919 on white or #f2f1ee on ink. The full field is for 64 px and up; below that the small cut, four by four with three lit, stands in (favicons, tabs). The app icon is the full field on an ink rounded square.",
      "heading": "The mark",
      "id": "4b11c6f9",
      "index": "a0"
    },
    "5ed88834": {
      "body": "Once, as it appears: the field scales in with the dramatic easing (about 900 ms). Then, only where the mark stands alone (the front page, a splash): 28 of the dots take turns being lit. Each grows from 5.5 to 13 over 0.6 s with ease-out (0.22, 1, 0.36, 1), stays lit for about 4 s, and shrinks back over 0.6 s, on a 12 s cycle with its own start, so about ten are lit at any moment and the picture never repeats in step. Nothing moves for people who ask for reduced motion: they see the still mark. Never animate the small cut or the app icon.",
      "heading": "How the mark moves",
      "id": "5ed88834",
      "index": "a1"
    }
  },
  "shapes": {},
